#: src/unsafe-rust/exercise.md:27
msgid "You will convert between all these types:"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-rust/exercise.md:29
msgid ""
"`&str` to `CString`: you need to allocate space for a trailing `\\0` "
"character,"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-rust/exercise.md:30
msgid "`CString` to `*const c_char`: you need a pointer to call C functions,"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-rust/exercise.md:31
msgid ""
"`*const c_char` to `&CStr`: you need something which can find the trailing "
"`\\0` character,"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-rust/exercise.md:33
msgid ""
"`&CStr` to `&[u8]`: a slice of bytes is the universal interface for \"some "
"unknown data\","
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-rust/exercise.md:35
msgid ""
"`&[u8]` to `&OsStr`: `&OsStr` is a step towards `OsString`, use [`OsStrExt`]"
"(https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/os/unix/ffi/trait.OsStrExt.html) to create it,"
msgstr ""

#: src/unsafe-rust/exercise.md:38
msgid ""
"`&OsStr` to `OsString`: you need to clone the data in `&OsStr` to be able to "
"return it and call `readdir` again."
msgstr ""

